<title>UK: UK economy strengthening, Clarke says.</title>
<headline>UK economy strengthening, Clarke says.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said in a statement the UK economy went from &quot;strength to strength&quot; in 1996 and the prospects for 1997 were even better.  </p>
<p>DATA SHOWED</p>
<p>=========== UK PRELIMINARY Q4 GDP +0.8% QQ, +2.6% YY, EX-OIL/GAS +0.7% QQ,</p>
<p>+2.5% YY</p>
<p>ONS SAYS TOTAL 1996 GDP GROWTH ESTIMATED AT 2.3%, EX-OIL GAS</p>
<p>+2.3%</p>
</text>
